  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The graph shows the variation with time <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t\"></span> of the velocity <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v\"></span> of two particles, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Q\"></span>, that start from the same position at <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t = 0\"></span> and move along the same straight line.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>Particle <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P\"></span> moves with a constant velocity <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"u\"></span>. Particle <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Q\"></span> moves with a constant acceleration from rest, reaching velocity <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"u\"></span> at time <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"T\"></span>.</p>\n<p>What is the time taken for particle <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Q\"></span> to overtake particle <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P\"></span>, and what is the velocity of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Q\"></span> at that instant?</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th></th><th>Time taken to overtake</th><th>Velocity of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Q\"></span></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr data-label=\"A\"><td>A</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"T\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"u\"></span></td></tr><tr data-label=\"B\"><td>B</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"T\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2u\"></span></td></tr><tr data-label=\"C\"><td>C</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2T\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"u\"></span></td></tr><tr data-label=\"D\"><td>D</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2T\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2u\"></span></td></tr></tbody></table>"
  },
